    "id": "p5-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "Let $f(x)=\\dfrac{x}{x^2+1}$. Show that $f\\left(\\dfrac1x\\right)=f(x)$, where $x\\ne0$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f\\left(\\dfrac1x\\right)=\\dfrac{x}{x^2+1}=f(x)$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)&=\\frac{1/x}{1/x^2+1}\\\\f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)&=\\frac{x}{1+x^2}\\\\f\\left(\\frac1x\\right)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
